  "unit": "Unit 11 - Lines",
  "description": "Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 11 - Lines for SAT Math preparation.",
  "duration": 45,
  "content": "<p><strong>Unit 11 - Lines — Title &amp; Goal</strong><br />Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 11 - Lines for SAT Math preparation.</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Slope (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></math>):</strong> measures steepness.  </li>\n</ul>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>rise</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>run</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>y-intercept (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></math>):</strong> point where line crosses <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></math>-axis.  </li>\n</ul>\n<p>Equation Form: </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong><br/>\nFind slope and intercept of line through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>Equation: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></math>. Plug <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math><br/>\nFinal: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.</p>\n<p>Try these on your own. Check your steps, not just the final answer.</p>\n<p>1) Find slope and intercept of line through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.\n2) Write equation of line with slope <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></math> through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.\n3) Find intersection of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>.\n<p><strong>Slope-Intercept Form</strong></p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>Point-Slope Form</strong></p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong><br/>\nEquation of line through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> with slope <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>\n<hr />\n<p>Solve system of equations.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 3</strong><br/>\nFind intersection of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>Set equal:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>Then <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math><br/>\nIntersection = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.</p>\n<hr />\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Parallel lines:</strong> same slope, different intercepts.  </li>\n<li><strong>Perpendicular lines:</strong> slopes multiply to <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> (negative reciprocals).  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example 4</strong><br/>\nFind equation of line parallel to <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>Slope = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>. Equation: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 5</strong><br/>\nFind equation of line perpendicular to <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>Slope = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math><br/>\nEquation: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⇒</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<hr />\n<ul>\n<li>Horizontal: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></math> (slope = 0).  </li>\n<li>Vertical: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></math> (slope undefined).  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example 6</strong><br/>\nEquation of line through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> and parallel to <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>:<br/>\nAnswer: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 7</strong><br/>\nEquation of line through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> and parallel to <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>:<br/>\nAnswer: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<hr />\n<ul>\n<li>Memorize slope formulas.  </li>\n<li>Parallel → same <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></math>.  </li>\n<li>Perpendicular → <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>·</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.  </li>\n<li>Watch out for vertical/horizontal lines.  </li>\n<li>For intersections, substitution is often faster than graphing.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>1) Find slope and intercept of line through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math><br/>\n2) Write equation of line with slope <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></math> through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math><br/>\n3) Find intersection of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n4) Write equation of line parallel to <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></math> through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math><br/>\n5) Write equation of line perpendicular to <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math> through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<hr />\n<p>1) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>. Equation: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>2) Point-slope: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⇒</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>3) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>. Intersection <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>4) Parallel slope <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>. Equation: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⇒</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>5) Perpendicular slope <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>. Equation: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⇒</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p><strong>More practice</strong></p>\n<p>Keep going—aim for accuracy first, then speed.</p>\n<p><strong>Mixed practice set</strong></p>\n<p>These mix everything above. Time yourself and reflect on any mistakes.</p>\n4) Write equation of line parallel to <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></math> through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.\n5) Write equation of line perpendicular to <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math> through <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.",
